\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Accuracy first, then what each answer costs. Bold marks the highest point estimate per model; where the 95\% intervals overlap, the difference is not significant (see the McNemar $p$ values in \cref  {tab:accuracy}). Context = median input tokens per question read by the agent model, and in \textsf  {C}{} separately by the broker's planner (\texttt  {llama-3.3-70b}); output = median output tokens of the agent model. Cost is the mean USD per question (provider-reported for frontier models, Workers AI list prices for open-weight models, planner included in \textsf  {C}{}); cost per correct answer is total cost divided by correct answers. $^{\dagger }$Includes runs whose planner usage was estimated from measured per-call usage.}}{35}{table.caption.93}\protected@file@percent }
